LAMMPS (10 Sep 2025)
  using 6 OpenMP thread(s) per MPI task
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# LAMMPS input: NVT MD with MACE-OFF23 (medium) ML interatomic potential
# Model: MACE-OFF23_medium.model-lammps.pt
#
# EDIT THESE BEFORE RUNNING:
#   1. "data.system"      -> your actual LAMMPS data file
#   2. the element list on the pair_coeff line -> must match, in order,
#      the atom TYPES you defined in your data file (a subset of the
#      10 elements MACE-OFF23 was trained on: H C N O F P S Cl Br I)
#   3. group/region/thermodynamic settings -> your actual system
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

units           metal
boundary        p p p
atom_style      atomic
atom_modify     map yes
newton          on off          # "newton on off" = newton_pair on, newton_bond off.
                                 # pair_style mace requires newton pair ON.
                                 # KOKKOS full-neighbor-list mode requires
                                 # newton bond OFF (moot anyway: atom_style
                                 # atomic has no bonded terms).

# ---- geometry / topology ----
read_data       data.system
Reading data file ...
  orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (16.925 16.925 16.925)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid
  reading atoms ...
  450 atoms
  read_data CPU = 0.011 seconds

# ---- MACE pair style ----
# no_domain_decomposition: recommended for a single MPI rank + threading
# (typical for small-to-medium systems). Drop it if you are running
# genuine multi-rank domain decomposition on a large system.
pair_style      mace no_domain_decomposition
pair_coeff      * * MACE-OFF23_medium.model-lammps.pt H C N O

# ---- neighbor settings ----
neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes

# ---- timestep ----
# MACE-OFF23 is an all-electron organic-chemistry potential with
# explicit H; use a conservative fs-scale timestep.
timestep        0.0005          # 0.5 fs

# ---- common variables ----
variable        Tinit  equal 300.0
variable        Trun   equal 300.0
variable        Patm   equal 1.01325     # 1 atm in bar (metal units use bar)

thermo_style    custom step temp pe ke etotal press vol density
thermo          10

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stage 0: energy minimization
# The packmol-packed box was placed with a finite distance tolerance,
# not energy-minimized, so there can be close contacts / large initial
# forces. Minimize before assigning velocities or running dynamics.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
min_style       cg
minimize        1.0e-6 1.0e-8 1000 10000
Generated 0 of 6 mixed pair_coeff terms from geometric mixing rule
Neighbor list info ...
  update: every = 1 steps, delay = 0 steps, check = yes
  max neighbors/atom: 2000, page size: 100000
  master list distance cutoff = 12
  ghost atom cutoff = 12
  binsize = 6, bins = 3 3 3
  1 neighbor lists, perpetual/occasional/extra = 1 0 0
  (1) pair mace, perpetual
      attributes: full, newton on
      pair build: full/bin/atomonly
      stencil: full/bin/3d
      bin: standard
